1. OWNERSHIP

   All intellectual property rights in RC Sails Scoring (the "Software")
   are exclusively owned by Stefano Ragusa (the "Owner"), including
   without limitation the source and object code, the scoring logic and
   architecture, the graphic design, user interface, colour and
   typographic choices, the layout of generated documents, the functional
   design, documentation and any derivative work thereof.

2. LICENCE GRANTED

   The Owner grants any person accessing the Software a free,
   non-exclusive, non-transferable and revocable licence, limited to using
   the application as published, for the purpose of scoring sailing races.

3. RESTRICTIONS

   Except with the Owner's prior written consent, it is expressly
   forbidden to copy, reproduce, republish, modify, adapt, translate,
   decompile, create derivative works of, distribute, sublicense, rent or
   sell the Software or any part of it; to remove or alter copyright
   notices; to reuse its graphic design or visual elements in other works;
   or to use the Software for commercial purposes.

4. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

   The Software includes third-party components governed by their own
   licences, listed in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. The restrictions in
   section 3 do not apply to those components.

5. NO WARRANTY

   The Software is provided "AS IS", without warranty of any kind. The
   Owner does not warrant that computed scores are free of errors or that
   they match the Notice of Race and Sailing Instructions of any given
   event. Verification of results remains the sole responsibility of the
   Race Committee.

6. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

   The Owner shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental or
   consequential damages arising from the use of or inability to use the
   Software, including loss of data or incorrect race results.

7. DATA

   The Software transmits no data to any server. All information entered
   remains on the user's device. The Owner collects no personal data.

8. GOVERNING LAW

   This licence is governed by Italian law.
